      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Today, we can treat osteoporotic patients with multiple drugs of various mechanisms and in various forms. Nevertheless, there exist few clinical evidences that exhibit an efficacy of an anti-osteoporotic drug on osteoporosis with pulmonary disorders, including asthma, COPD and OSAS. We should use drugs for osteoporotic patients with pulmonary disorders in accordance with a guideline on the management and treatment of glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis or a guideline on the management and treatment of osteoporosis, according to whether they are treated by glucocorticoid or not."},
